  </div>
  <div class="post-content">

<p><strong>Neo Calendar</strong> is a personal, read-only Google Calendar integration that runs on <a href="/">Neo</a> — an AI assistant on a Raspberry Pi 5 in South London.</p>

<h2>What it does</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Reads calendar events (read-only) to prepare a daily briefing each morning.</li>
  <li>Checks upcoming appointments, family events, and shared calendars.</li>
  <li>Never creates, modifies, or deletes events.</li>
  <li>Runs entirely on private home hardware — no third-party processing.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data &amp; privacy</h2>

<p>Only your calendar events are accessed, and only in read-only mode, to generate briefings. Access is granted through Google's standard OAuth consent screen and can be revoked at any time from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions page</a>. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p>Questions about Neo Calendar? Contact the app owner via the blog.</p>

